Verify existing reply IDs and append exact\-context readback evidence. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post performance outcomes\fR
Inspect or import explicit receipt\-linked enquiries, sign\-ups and sales. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post accounts list\fR
Inspect additional identities, activation and credential presence. Consequence: READ_ONLY.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post accounts import\fR
Preview or add inactive X/Threads/LinkedIn identities, project aliases and independent budgets. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post accounts connect\fR
Verify credentials for an inactive additional account, including non\-secret reuse of the existing LinkedIn member credential for a Page actor. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. --reuse-default is accepted only for LinkedIn organization/organizationBrand actors and stores no copied access token; the Page is still verified independently before enablement.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post accounts enable\fR
Preview or enable an independently budgeted account after identity verification. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post accounts disable\fR
Disable future use of an additional account; existing effects remain recorded. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post operations\fR
Observe project or portfolio milestones and optionally save a private report. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --save. --all joins each registered project's generated, brief and vault schedules to exact receipts. Saved by the bounded collector; no provider call, publication or repair.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post campaign receipts\fR
Join reviewed brief schedules to publication receipts. Consequence: READ_ONLY.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post campaign reconcile\fR
Preview or perform bounded GET\-only reconciliation of existing publication effects. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. --apply performs read-only provider GETs and writes separate reconciliation evidence; it never publishes, retries, resets or deletes.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault register\fR
Preview or register designated document authority. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. --enable trusts approved entries from this document's editors; apply requires reviewed hash.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault extend\fR
Review adding a provider destination without replacing existing vault authority. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Apply requires a review hash covering current policy, account identities and document copy. Existing destinations cannot be replaced.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault sync\fR
Observe approved vault revisions and withdrawals; admit new packages within destination budgets. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault status\fR
Read vault configuration and local observations. Consequence: READ_ONLY.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault coverage\fR
Reconcile expected vault projects and platform entries with local authority, freshness and intact imports. Consequence: READ_ONLY. No Google read or repair. HOLD projects stay outside expected publishing coverage; imports do not prove publication.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault credentials\fR
Install private operator\-owned Google refresh credentials. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post vault auth\fR
Connect read\-only Google access using Desktop OAuth and PKCE. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post evidence check\fR
Preview or observe a scoped revision\-bound HTTPS JSON application check. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post performance review\fR
Compare receipt\-linked metrics at matching post ages and destinations. Consequence: READ_ONLY.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post performance capture\-due\fR
Preview or capture metrics near a target post age. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post campaign brief\fR
Compile and preview or import reviewed evidence briefs with distinct editorial angles. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Apply requires the reviewed input hash. Manual-only by default; --allocate opts into existing scheduling policy. Evidence references are not independently verified; full rendered copy needs review.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source receipts\fR
Find matching scheduled publication receipts for a project's generated source campaigns. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Local JSON across source revisions; no provider call. A direct or brief-imported campaign does not complete the generated-source milestone. Pending is not failure.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source evidence\fR
Read exact\-commit GitHub workflow and deployment observations. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Optional --sha must be a full commit SHA. JSON report; no cursor, copy or authority changes. Missing observations are not negative proof or production verification.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post campaign explain\fR
Explain local copy provenance, allocation exclusions, schedules and receipts. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Local snapshot only. No GitHub/provider calls. Expected account binding is not live identity verification.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source import\fR
Preview or register an inactive runtime GitHub source policy. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Add-only registration. --apply requires the reviewed input_sha256. Does not fetch GitHub or enable replenishment.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source list\fR
Read runtime source policies and activation state as JSON. Consequence: READ_ONLY.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source preview\fR
Read GitHub and preview exact static copy, bound identities and the event policy. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Returns review_sha256. No campaigns, cursors or schedules are written.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source enable\fR
Authorise a runtime source for future replenishment and allocator selection. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE. Requires --expected-sha256 from a fresh source preview. Pins repository identity and baselines existing commits. No immediate social post.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post replenish source disable\fR
Stop new replenishment from a runtime source. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE. Existing campaigns and reservations remain authorised; cancel unwanted schedules separately.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post registry import\fR
Preview or add a runtime project with expected account bindings. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. --apply requires the reviewed input SHA-256. Add-only local authority; does not connect accounts or import credentials.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post campaign import\fR
Preview or add approved runtime copy, with explicit optional allocator opt\-in. Consequence: FUTURE_CONSEQUENCE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. --apply requires the reviewed input SHA-256. No provider call. --allocate explicitly authorises future selection by the running portfolio allocator. Omit --allocate for manual-only copy.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post health\fR
Inspect local publishing evidence, freshness, capacity and automation health. Consequence: READ_ONLY. No provider calls or repair. Exit 0=ok, 1=warning, 2=unknown, 3=attention. See docs/HEALTH.md.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post doctor\fR
Check local prerequisites and stored configuration state. Consequence: READ_ONLY.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup interactive\fR
Run the resumable fresh/explore terminal setup wizard. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Bare 'ocpf-post setup' is an alias. Creates only bootstrap-local setup state; never connects providers, installs services or enables publishing.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup admission\fR
Prove host capabilities and classify existing installation state before guided setup. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Reads bootstrap/runtime authority evidence only. Production mode additionally requires a reachable systemd user manager; no provider call or mutation occurs.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup browser\fR
Serve the secure loopback\-only browser renderer over the same SetupEngine. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: close the browser without applying reviewed actions. The listener is fixed to 127.0.0.1 and uses a process-local session plus CSRF/origin checks. Starting the renderer changes no authority; browser forms preserve each underlying setup command's preview/review/apply gate.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup beta\fR
Enroll, observe, inspect or decide an explicitly bounded local beta ring. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: --action status. Beta evidence is private, append-only and hash-chained. Rehearsal cannot unlock runtime adoption review; only an owner-canary decision can become bootstrap-runtime-adoption ready. The command never enables publishing authority by itself.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup adoption\-review\fR
Build an evidence\-backed package for this project's own Post\-Once\-derived runtime adoption. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Returns BLOCKED unless the owner-canary beta decision is BOOTSTRAP_RUNTIME_ADOPTION_READY. AyobamiH/post-once and the operator's existing local Post-Once are permanently outside the mutation path.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup start\fR
Start fresh, explore, or same\-operator source setup from explicit inputs. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. The source identity can be used for healthy migration or immutable recovery points. Dead-host recovery itself starts from setup restore --recovery.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup status\fR
Read the latest or named bootstrap setup session and control\-store health. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Opens an existing setup database read-only and does not create one when missing.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup resume\fR
Resume one incomplete setup session from its last committed revision. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Uses durable revision-checked transitions; never restarts or replaces an existing session silently.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup export\fR
Preview or seal a credential\-free healthy migration bundle from a quiescent source. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. --apply retires only the bootstrap source authority model after writer-unit quiescence is observed, then seals an immutable bundle. It never stops services, copies credentials or calls a provider.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup recovery\-point\fR
Preview or seal an immutable credential\-free point for later dead\-host recovery. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Requires a quiescent source and exact review hash. Sealing never retires the source, changes provider credentials, re-arms schedules or enables publishing.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup inspect\-bundle\fR
Verify a healthy migration or dead\-host recovery artifact without granting authority. Consequence: READ_ONLY. Use --recovery for recovery points. Verification materializes only bounded quarantine state; production roots are untouched.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup restore\fR
Verify and quarantine a healthy migration bundle or dead\-host recovery point on a new installation. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. --recovery requires an explicit source-loss time and acceptable data-loss window. Recovery marks the old installation unknown and never activates the target.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup verify\fR
Verify target provider identity evidence and reconcile migration/recovery schedules. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Use --recovery for a dead-host target. Milestone G stops at RECOVERY_REVIEW_READY with stale-host authority explicitly unresolved; no service activation or provider consequence.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup verify\-fresh\fR
Read\-only verify a connected provider plus user\-owned project/content before fresh activation. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Provider observation is read-only: no refresh or publication. The exact immutable account ID must match and standalone runtime state must contain a user-owned project plus an enabled source or imported campaign. Historical packaged owner defaults never satisfy this gate.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup connect\-x\fR
Connect and read\-back verify one X account for Fresh beta onboarding. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Runs OAuth Authorization Code + PKCE, then proves the exact account through a read-only identity request. A prompted/file client secret is persisted only after successful authorization. No post, schedule, source activation or unattended-automation activation occurs.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup onboard\-x\fR
Bind the connected X identity to one user project and manual\-only campaign, then advance Fresh verification. Consequence: LOCAL_STATE_WRITE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Preview is non-mutating. --apply performs reviewed add-only local project/campaign imports with allocator opt-in disabled, then uses read-only provider readiness to advance to verification_ready. It never publishes or activates unattended automation.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup activate\fR
Preview or apply the unattended\-publishing activation gate. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Apply requires an exact review hash. State/config promotion and timer staging occur while the local automation marker is inactive; the marker write is the final cutover. Recovery requires structured resolution of every recovery-review blocker.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post setup deactivate\fR
Preview or apply marker\-first unattended\-automation deactivation. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Safe inspection: omit --apply. Apply writes the local automation marker inactive before disabling timers. Durable receipts/schedules are never rolled backwards.
.TP
\fBocpf\-post x auth\fR
Run X OAuth 2.0 Authorization Code + PKCE. Consequence: AUTHORITY_CHANGE. Changes local provider authorisation state.
